        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/16/meta-ai-can-now-alert-parents-when-their-teens-discuss-self-harm/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/07/Meta-AI-teen-self-harm-alerts.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\"><a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/meta/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Meta</a> has announced that parents can receive alerts when their teens discuss suicide or other forms of self-harm with its AI on <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/instagram/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Instagram</a>, <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/guides/facebook/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noreferrer noopener\">Facebook</a>, or Meta Horizons.</p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">You’ll need to opt in to Meta’s supervision tools for parents and guardians in order to select the family accounts you want to supervise …</p>",
