        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/20/apple-releases-first-ios-26-6-rc-for-iphone/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2026/05/iOS-26.6-rc.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\n</p><h1 class=\"h1\" style=\"box-sizing: inherit; margin-top: 0.67em; margin-right: 0px; margin-left: 0px; font-size: var(--fs-38); white-space: normal;\"></h1>\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">While iOS 27 is very much the new focus for pre-release software, Apple is still preparing iOS 26.6 as the next iPhone update. Apple has released the first release candidate for iOS 26.6. iOS 26.6 beta has <a href=\"https://9to5mac.com/2026/05/26/apple-releases-first-ios-26-6-beta-for-iphone/\">been in testing</a> since the end of May.</p>",
        "type": "Technology",
