        "title": "Apple raises prices for Apple Music and Apple One subscriptions",
        "url": "https://9to5mac.com/2026/07/17/apple-raises-prices-for-apple-music-and-apple-one-subscriptions/",
        "content_text": "<div class=\"feat-image\"><img src=\"https://9to5mac.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/6/2025/10/apple-one-premier-blue.jpg?quality=82&#038;strip=all&#038;w=1600\" /></div><p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has raised the price of <a href=\"https://apple.co/48lJx2o\">Apple Music today</a> in the United States and other countries. Starting today, Apple Music’s Individual plan now costs $11.99 per month, up from $10.99. </p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Apple has also increased the price of select Apple One bundles. </p>\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">In a statement to <em>9to5Mac</em>, Apple said: “As a result of rising licensing costs, Apple Music is increasing its subscription price beginning today.”</p>",
